Step 2: Render par Backend Deploy Karein
render.com par jayein aur GitHub se sign up / login karein.

Dashboard par New + button par click karke Web Service chunein.

Apna backend GitHub repository select karein aur connect karein.

Form me ye details bharein:

Name: Apne project ka naam (jaise: my-django-api)

Language: Python 3

Branch: main (ya master)

Build Command: ./build.sh

Start Command:
gunicorn <project_name>.wsgi:application	

Create Web Service par click karein.









---------
Step 3: React Frontend Setup (VS Code me)
API Base URL check karein:
Apne React project me jahan bhi aapne Axios ya fetch me [http://127.0.0.1:8000](http://127.0.0.1:8000) ya localhost:8000 likha tha, us URL ko badal kar apne Render backend ka link daal dein:

JavaScript
// Example
const API_BASE_URL = "https://my-django-api.onrender.com";
Build test karein:
VS Code terminal me React folder me run karein:

Bash
npm run build
(Agar bina error ke build ban rahi hai, toh project deploy ke liye ready hai).

GitHub par push karein:
Frontend project ko ek alag GitHub repository me commit aur push kar dein.

Step 4: Vercel par Frontend Deploy Karein
vercel.com par jayein aur GitHub se login karein.

Add New... par click karke Project chunein.

Apna React frontend repository select karein aur Import par click karein.

Settings me:

Framework Preset: Vite ya Create React App (Vercel khud detect kar leta hai).

Root Directory check karein (agar repo ke andar subfolder hai toh choose karein, warna blank chhod dein).

Deploy button par click karein.

1 minute ke andar aapki website live ho jayegi aur aapko ek link mil jayega (jaise [https://your-project.vercel.app](https://your-project.vercel.app)).








