File Save Karein:Ctrl + S daba kar file save karein.2. Syntax aur Rules (Kaise likha jata hai)Folder Ignore Karna: Kisi bhi folder ke naam ke aage hamesha slash / lagayein (e.g., node_modules/). Isse us folder ke andar ki saari sub-files ignore ho jati hain.Extension Wise Ignore (* Wildcard): Agar kisi specific extension ki sabhi files ignore karni hon, toh asterisk lagayein:*.pyc $\rightarrow$ saari compiled python files ignore hongi.*.log $\rightarrow$ saare log files ignore honge.Comment Dena (#): Kisi line ke aage # lagane par Git use comment manta hai aur read nahi karta (e.g., # React Files).Exception Rule (! Negation): Agar aapne poora folder ignore kiya hai par usme se koi ek file track karni hai:Plaintextsecrets/
!secrets/example.txt
Root vs Sub-directory:Agar aap likhte hain node_modules/, toh Git root aur har sub-folder (jaise frontend/node_modules/) me use ignore karega.3. Sabse Zaroori Dhyan Rakhne Yogya Baateingit add . chalane se pehle banana zaroori:Git sirf un files ko ignore karta hai jo untracked (pehle kabhi track na hui hon).Agar aapne .gitignore banane se pehle hi git add . ya git commit kar diya tha, toh .gitignore me naam daalne ke baad bhi Git use ignore nahi karega.Agar galti se file pehle track ho chuki ho toh Solution:
Agar db.sqlite3 ya node_modules pehle hi Git cache me chala gaya hai, toh VS Code terminal me ye commands run karein:Bashgit rm -r --cached .
git add .
git commit -m "Fix .gitignore tracking"
(Yeh command aapke local PC se files delete nahi karti, sirf Git ke tracking memory/index se hata deti hai).Sensitive Files kabhi push na karein:.env file ko hamesha .gitignore me rakhein taaki aapki secret keys, database passwords aur API tokens public GitHub par leak na hon.Production Database:Local SQLite database file (db.sqlite3) ko Git me push nahi karna chahiye, kyunki production deployment (Render) par database migrations ke through fresh setup hota hai.   
